WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.000
-Drew!
-Hi!

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.501
-Oh, my gosh!
We love you.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.367
-I love you.
Thank you so much

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.534
for coming back to the show.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:09.000
Thank you for doing "Ew!"
-I mean...

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.200
-You brought it back.
-I have this one little bag

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.834
of "Ew."
It's like merch.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.334
-You do.
-And I have carried it with me

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.701
for five, six years.
-Every time you come over,

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.100
every time that you hang out,
you pull out this little purse

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.334
that says, "Ew."
-Yes, that's --

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.334
It was my way
of being close to the sketch.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.701
And I wanted to be
in that room so badly.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.534
It's my favorite on the show,

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:31.868
and now I got to be
a part of it.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.133
-Come on, buddy.
-Thank you!

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.200
You know I love you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.667
Oh, I --
No, I know.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.934
You had a big night
last night, my pal.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:43.033
You were honored --
the Time 100 Gala.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:46.601
You were one of the most
influential people in the world.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:49.801
-I don't see it that way,
but I'm very glad they do.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.968
-I think they do.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.067
-I've never been on that list.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:58.200
It's a beautiful --
an extraordinary list to be on.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.234
But, really, I got to actually
make the whole evening

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.467
not about me,
which is very much not about me,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:07.834
but I got to really spend it
honoring someone else, actually.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.834
-Yeah, here you are here
with Steven Spielberg.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.100
-No big deal.
-Yep. Yeah.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.501
-And Ke Huy Quan.
-Yep.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.934
[ Applause ]

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:21.534
What's so meaningful
about this is, Ke and I met

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.334
on the set of "Temple of Doom,"

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.634
"Indiana Jones
and the Temple of Doom."

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:27.067
-No way.
-Absolutely. I came to London

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.234
to hang out for around a week.

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.934
Ke and I went
to the zoo together.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.067
We hung out.
And, you know, I would --

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.200
I would spend my time
with Steven,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.267
and he would just bring me
to work with him, and --

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.567
-How old were you guys?

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:44.234
I think I was like 8 or 9,
and he was like 11 or 12.

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.834
-Is that cool to be right here?

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:48.234
-And he still has pictures
of us at the zoo,

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:51.033
and we would hang out.
I loved him so much.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.601
I mean, "Goonies," Data.
-Yeah. Hello.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.534
Yeah, I know.
He's unbelievable.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:58.300
-And he was such a good person,
and I liked him so much.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.067
And there we are.
It's like, you know --

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:03.434
And Steven is the type
of incredible human being

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:07.400
that I think just wants to know,
like, all of his kids are okay.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.000
And so it just felt like
this wonderful moment

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.334
where we could be like,
"Your kids are okay."

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.234
-Kids are doing all right.
Yeah, absolutely. Yeah.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.400
You're doing pretty well.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.000
I have so many things
to talk to you about

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.300
and congratulate you on.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.801
You are nominated for
a Daytime Emmy Award, buddy,

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:26.667
for Outstanding Daytime
Talk Series Host!

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.767
Emmy?!
What are you talkin--

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.100
And then the show was nominated
for six other nominations.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.300
-Yeah, yeah, yeah!
-Wow!

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.734
-Yeah, I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:39.300
I am fully convinced
that a cartoon Acme piano

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.534
is going to fall from the sky
and land on my head.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.367
It's too good to be true!

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.834
-And you got renewed
for season four.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.167
-Yes!
-Dude, what is --

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.934
how do you feel about all
this -- all this success?

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.734
-I don't feel
very comfortable with it

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.467
because it just seems
too good to be true.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.167
But I will try to take it in.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.000
-You put the work in.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.767
-I feel very grateful.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:01.834
You know, listen,
life is a roller coaster,

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:05.467
and if it's on an ascend
for a little while,

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.667
just try to enjoy it.
I think. I'm trying so hard.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:12.300
I'm more used to,
honestly, tougher news.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.367
Like, does anyone else
feel like that?

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.234
[ Applause ]
Like, when things are good,

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:18.767
you're like, "What's wrong?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.834
-Yeah.
-I'm used to tougher news.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.267
And so -- And I'm used
to working at it,

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:27.267
and I'm just happy that there's
some good news on the horizon.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.868
It's great for everyone
who builds the show

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.067
because we all do it together.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:34.567
I said, "I will never call
this my show.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.334
There's no I.
It's ours and we.

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.133
We launched in a pandemic.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.400
Somehow we've made it through.
It's a miracle.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.634
-Yeah, buddy.
You're doing great.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:44.133
-It's a miracle!
-You do a great job.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.567
-It's -- It's --

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:49.033
This -- This isn't easy to do,
I found out.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.767
I mean, I didn't think
it was going to be easy,

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:56.167
but I thought maybe my life
would help with some training.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.467
You know, maybe --

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.701
Oh, I've been doing this
since I was 11 months old.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:02.267
Like, "I'll be able
to do this job."

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.167
-It's a different --
totally different animal.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.767
-Oh, yeah.
-When we were talking,

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.467
when you were like, "I think
I might do this talk thing,"

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:08.868
I go --
You're like, "What's up?"

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.501
I go, "It's a lot of work."

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:16.367
-You warned me, and -- and I
have so much respect for this.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.200
And I -- you know,
look, I've also, like,

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.968
been on the other side
of interviews my whole life.

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:26.267
Not here. Like when you're at
a round table of, you know --

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:29.701
There's all different kinds
of interviews and conversations.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.667
You're more of
a conversationalist.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.367
You take the armor off
piece by piece, you have fun.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.267
There's no gotchas here.
-No.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.834
-And I just wanted to try
and sort of think about

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:43.234
what I felt like my whole life
and how I'd be so excited

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:45.467
if someone asked me,
like, a different question

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.734
or there was good energy
in the room,

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:51.400
or if it didn't feel
like I'm sitting here

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.767
asking you a question,

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.734
but I'm not going to reveal
anything about myself.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.934
-But you get up close
and personal.

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:02.067
-I think I've indexed in
the complete opposite extreme.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.934
-You get really
up close and personal.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.567
This is -- This is you
interviewing Brooke Shields.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:06.934
Look at this.
You guys are basically,

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.300
like, spooning, almost.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, and we got much closer

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.634
than that
at certain points, too.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:16.334
-Yeah.
-I'm on my knees, I'm hugging.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.067
-Yeah.
Here's Chloe Bailey right here.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.734
Look at this one.
-Yep, yep. That's --

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.634
-Yeah, you're doing --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:24.234
You can't sit in your chair.
-No, I feel...

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:27.567
-You get in there.
-...this magnetic pull of, like,

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:31.234
you know, I -- I...

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.901
My therapist would say, like,

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:36.000
"You're not supposed
to be attached to things."

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.334
But, Barry,
I'm so attached to this.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.234
I love doing this show so much.

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:42.300
I get to learn
from people every day.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.200
I get to have
these incredible conversations

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.067
that I definitely
take something away with.

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:49.567
It's always improving my life.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.000
It's -- It's profound.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.901
It's fun.
We like to be silly.

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.067
It's whiplash comedy
because that's like life.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:59.133
Like, the heavier it gets,
the more you want to laugh.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:00.734
-But, yeah. But you're
interested in people,

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.267
and you're interested in things.
-I love people.

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:04.267
I love every human being
on the planet.

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:07.367
I'm fascinated.
And everyone has a story,

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.634
and every person is exceptional
and interesting,

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:14.267
and it is so fun
to literally get to be

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.567
a conversationalist at work.

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:18.367
It's the coolest thing
in the world.

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:20.133
-There's a meme
going around online

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:23.501
about how your interviews
are so up close.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.334
-I know. I actually
really am into this.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.067
-This one made me laugh.
Like, this one.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.868
-Yeah.
-"The guest -- Can I be honest?"

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.601
-Yep. Yep.

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:36.200
-Their eyeballs are touching.
-No, I know.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.734
-Their eyeballs are touching.
-I know.

00:06:38.734 --> 00:06:41.267
At first, I was like,
"Oh, is this a good thing?

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.501
I can't tell."

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.000
And then I was like,
"No, this is awesome!"

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.801
-Yeah, it's a great thing!
-It's so much fun.

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:49.100
Can I ask you a question?
-Yeah, of course.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:52.734
-Like, what's your favorite
thing about getting to do this?

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:56.934
This privilege, this crazy,
amazing world of a job?

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:59.067
-I think --
That's a great question.

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:01.033
There's so many great things
that come with this.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:03.200
I think it's making
the audience laugh.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.567
I think it's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.601
-See, that's the best.

00:07:06.601 --> 00:07:08.467
And seeing their face.

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:10.601
It feels good.
And to see someone laughing.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:13.367
Like, you know,
you have a real laugh face.

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:15.667
You have a fake laugh face
where you're like, "Ha ha."

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.701
And then if something's
really funny, you're like...

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.133
And it's like --
I love that face.

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.968
I like someone making
that ugly laugh face.

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:22.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:25.567
-And connection, you know?
To be connected together.

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:27.901
-I love it.
I love the live of it all.

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:30.534
I mean, we did shows in COVID
with no audience,

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:32.667
and, gosh,
I missed you guys so much.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.934
-I was here.
I came for one.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:38.067
-And I've been, you know,
an actor and a producer.

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:41.501
And it's a really quiet job.
Like, you're around people,

00:07:41.501 --> 00:07:43.734
but it's very insular.
You're kind of inside your head.

00:07:43.734 --> 00:07:44.934
You drive home at night,
and you're like,

00:07:44.934 --> 00:07:47.133
"What did I just do today?"
That was wild.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.801
And this is
the most connective...

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:52.167
Like, there's a cacophony,
there's an energy.

00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.801
Like, I'm not a musician.

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:56.033
I've never been
in a job like this.

00:07:56.033 --> 00:08:00.300
And for our first year, we were
like cable access on premium TV.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:05.000
It was just me talking to myself
by myself and, you know...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.767
And now we have
a full audience and --

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:10.701
-And look at you getting
nominated for all these Emmys.

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:12.133
That's what I'm talking about,
bud.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:13.434
-I'm just --
-Well done.

00:08:13.434 --> 00:08:16.501
-I'm very --
-Well deserved.

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:19.868
And now you're hosting
the MTV Movie &amp; TV Awards

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:22.901
live, Sunday, May 7th.
-I know.

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:24.033
-Are you ready for this?
Are you nervous?

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.167
-I'm so ready.
We're filming --

00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:28.033
You know, when, like,
MTV used to, like,

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:30.000
bring you actually
into the movies

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.000
and the amazing films
that they would make?

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.167
-You're doing that?
-We're doing all of it!

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:35.801
-Oh, I love that!
-It's gonna be so much fun!

00:08:35.801 --> 00:08:38.100
-That's my favorite!
That's my favorite thing.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.334
-Mine, too!
And I loved it so much.

00:08:40.334 --> 00:08:42.167
And they're the most
amazing people to work with.

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:43.467
It's an incredible show.

00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:45.701
There's incredible people
coming.

00:08:45.701 --> 00:08:49.634
And if there's one thing that
I definitely want to celebrate

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:52.601
in this world and life,
it's film and television.

00:08:52.601 --> 00:08:54.400
-Yeah, movies and TV.
-Yes!

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.734
-I love it.
-That's what I want to do

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:58.267
at the end of the day, too.
-Yeah.

00:08:58.267 --> 00:08:59.567
-And I just -- I'm so excited.

00:08:59.567 --> 00:09:01.467
-Congrats on every single thing.
Thank you for being here.

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:02.767
Thank you for playing,
as always.

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.234
You're always the best guest.
I love you so much.

00:09:04.234 --> 00:09:05.868
-Oh, my gosh.
-Congrats on everything.

00:09:05.868 --> 00:09:07.701
Drew Barrymore, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.701 --> 00:09:13.133
-The MTV Movie &amp; TV Awards
are May 7th at 8:00 p.m. on MTV.

